{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341570-experimentation","id":1341570,"title":"Experimentation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-15T21:18:03-07:00","id":1341570,"title":"Experimentation","content":"Are there rules or suggestions for Experimentation anywhere in the history of the line? I see lots of references to this or that experiment resulted in whatever. But what if it is the players who want to do the experimenting? I want to house rule something for a game anyway, but I am trying to find anything already out there that I can chop up and mix together.<br /> <br /> My basic idea for a House Rule, thinking in a vacuum, is to have the player tell me in basic terms what he is trying to accomplish and why the character believes that this can be done (dig into the Paradigm). I come up with an unreasonable number of successes required and let them get to work. It may take many multiple rolls (of whatever) to get there, and in between each stage of the experiment they need to do field research. This is where the stories come from. Gather shards from the Avatar Storm, get a live dragon egg, break into a Technocrats lab and steal his research, get yours stolen! and so on.<br /> <br /> This is a very rough-draft idea. I came up with it just now as I wrote this post, and looking at it, it has major flaws. Is there a better rule out there?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T12:44:42-07:00","id":1341686,"title":"","content":"Experiments used for what purpose? Creating a wonder? Making a chimera? Learn Knowledge and Skills?<br /> <br /> This could be interesting to roleplay a PC learning a new level for a sphere. Or even, learning the first dot of a sphere with a teacher of a very different paradigm, since you need to adapt it to your field.<br /> <br /> Actually being a researcher myself, psychology, doing said experiments look really close to what I do in real life, and so as I gm I find it really fun to see my players experimenting, testing and probing the world deeper than: &quot; I use level 1 (insert any sphere) to check it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T18:58:14-07:00","id":1341755,"title":"","content":"The player defines their purpose I suppose. I can think of many ideas. In simple game terms, I guess it comes in three stages. You want to understand something that is not yet known, You want to do something that cannot yet be done, or You want to do something in a way that is easier and/or avoids the normal hazards. The concept works for Mystics and Technomancers and Technocrats alike.<br /> <br /> Examples could include:<br /> * Inventing a Rote that bends the normal limits of the Spheres and/or their Paradigm.<br /> * Figuring out how to predict Avatar Storms and protect from them.<br /> * Discovering a method to manipulate Paradox for potential benefit (using the Scorge &amp; Fortune system from Sorcerers Crusade)<br /> * Create a Wonder that breaks normal rules, such as various story McGuffins scattered about cannon.<br /> * Rediscover Archmastery, invent a new Sphere (of minor effects probably), ceate a new method for magick, and soon.<br /> <br /> What I would want, beyond a repeating cycle of adventure/roll/adventure/roll, is something that will potentially randomize results. You may know what you are looking for, but you don't know what you may find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T21:27:46-07:00","id":1341779,"title":"","content":"Minor Spheres are pretty fun, but I wouldn't say the rote should break the rules of the game. The default rotes given and exampled in the Traditions books, and the Technocracy books, are excessive and require a lot of experimentation on their own. Some require extremely expensive materials, others require extensive time. What bonus do they offer?:<br /> None, that's simply how the Rote/effect is done. (Purity of resources/extensive research can give bonuses however)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T09:55:09-07:00","id":1342736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . The default rotes given and exampled in the Traditions books, and the Technocracy books, are excessive and require a lot of experimentation on their own. Some require extremely expensive materials, others require extensive time. What bonus do they offer?:<br /> None, that's simply how the Rote/effect is done. </div> </div> </div>A few of those do grant &quot;bonuses&quot;, or cause effects that can't be deduced <i>entirely </i>from the general rules.<br /> <br /> Like the Etherite Matter 5 &quot;antimatter&quot; Rote (from the Revised Tradition book), allowing to create a substance that causes successes x3 of damage (instead of 2, albeit you need to get the sucesses to summon the stuff first).<br /> <br /> Or the Euthanatos Rote that sacrifices the mage using it to conjure an explosion, and allows to expend all your Quintessence to add levels of damage to the total (rather than merely lower the difficulty)<br /> <br /> Or the variant time travel of the Etherites that transports you to alternate timelines (that we didn't even knew existed before that Rote was published...unless they're the Mirror Zone in which case nothing in the rules clearly stated out that you can enter there without Spirit, until that Rote was invented. So the point would stand).<br /> <br /> All of these from the top of my head. There are more RAW rotes that represent a RAW breaking of the RAW, or at least an expansion of what can be deduced from *just* reading the core rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-21-2019, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T12:33:55-07:00","id":1342776,"title":"","content":"That is my point exactly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> What if one of my players wants to be the one to invent the cool new trick, such as one of those examples? But different, someone else already did that. It isn't about having more power. It is about the pride and prestige of accomplishment. It is a McGuffin to hook a chronicle on. Yet the results have to be tangible, something that motivates gamer psychology.<br /> If there isn't such a rule, I would ask for help creating one. I don't want to hand wave it or reduce it to steps x-y-z. There is comfort in rules, and gamers derive enjoyment from the &quot;crunch&quot; (if flavored just right). Rules grant the player freedom to imagine strategy. A sandbox as opposed to a railroad. As part of the gaming social contract, the GM has to abide by the rule as agreed to. Thus, instead of a list of steps, it becomes a McGuffin to inspire stories.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T06:56:38-07:00","id":1342936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341570-experimentation?p=1342776#post1342776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there isn't such a rule. </div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't such a rule.<br /> <br /> There are rules about research allowing to gain xp, but not about <i>characters </i>creating stuff that bend the rules (be these minor/alternate spheres or &quot;especial&quot; rotes). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would ask for help creating one </div> </div> </div>Such a rule would need to be, I think, deeply soaked with ST fiat (hand waving). We're talking about <i>players </i>creating exceptions to the normal RAW <i>(</i>even w/o entering into &quot;odd&quot; Rotes). <br /> <br /> Think about creating Thaumaturgy rituals in Vampire, or Lore rituals in Demon, or new Sorcery in Exalted. The process itself has steps (xp expenditure, time consumption, etc.) but the end result it's only very loosely limited by a general &quot;vive&quot; of the amount of power a spell at such level should have. The end result of these endeavors are indistinguishable from House Rules (these activities being part of the RAW notwithstanding)<br /> <br /> Ultimately would need to determine if these &quot;special&quot; spheres and rotes that the player wants are balanced. The <i>process </i>can be ruled, but the end result can't (or, rather, one would need to create new Mage system that can expain those odd ends in order to rule the end result. Pretty hard thing to do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T10:42:15-07:00","id":1342967,"title":"","content":"Ars Magica has a pretty solid system for experimentation, both for casual developments and breakthrough discoveries. I could adapt and plug that into a game, but it would feel off. different mechanics. In that game it is a modifier to your lab total and a roll of a single die on a chart. Mage works on dice pools, and for aesthetics, any side system should also work using a pool. Switching a mechanic back and forth causes a disconnect in suspension of disbelief.<br /> Fiat hand waving can be avoided by writing a rule. The hand-wavy part is in the writing, and then it is done.<br /> <br /> I am thinking about your suggestion of deep xp investing though. You have to go out and obtain insight (research and adventure). The xp gained, only spend part on yourself, the rest on your Experiment. The idea is that you have to score &quot;x&quot; number of successes in your Lab, and in order to keep the roll going, you have to dump research/insight into the project. The gm can award bonus insight points for clever insight ideas and good story interaction.<br /> The number of successes needed should be a huge number, which depends on the magnitude of the breakthrough you are trying to achieve. Instead of pure fiat, set some benchmarks. The player discusses the idea with the gm, and come to an agreement beforehand as to what mark is being aimed for. Say like, 25 successes for something trivial (a rote with tweaky mechanics, like from first edition, or something another faction/tradition can do but you can't), 50 for something minor but significant (a new minor sphere or something), 100 for something Major (a cure for vampires).<br /> What else?<br /> You gotta spend 1xp for each die you roll, and you can only roll a maximum of your Arete. Maybe invent a Merit that can increase that cap.<br /> Along the way, keep track of the total number of 1's and 10's rolled. A botched roll can ruin the experiment. Kind of like extended Ritual rolls. But even if you don't botch, an excessive number of 1's over the long term will start to warp and/or detract from what you are trying to accomplish. For example, you are trying to find a way to use Spirit in place of Prime to fuel Forces effects. I'd put that at Minor (50 successes). You get there, but along the way you accumulated twenty-five &quot;1's&quot;. A benchmark of half, So say it &quot;greatly Weakens or Alters Results&quot;. Perhaps you can use Spirit 4 in place of Prime 2 now, or you figured out how to use Prime with Forces and Spirit to empower a spirit with a Forces based charm it did not already have (which is probably something you can already do, or just make a Fetish to do that).<br /> This is all a brainstorm, but I hope you can see what I am getting at. Remember, it is not about the power, it is about plot and prestige.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T11:39:06-07:00","id":1342982,"title":"","content":"As an idea for a crunchy system, I would have a number of &quot;experimentation points&quot; or some sort of threshold that can abstract investigation. That way, the cuality of the research can be directly related to the chances of succeeding.<br /> <br /> For instance: You want to invent a Rote to cure vampirism and I say the treshold it's 100. Ok, so, on your researches you want to find blood of vampires to understand the Curse. I could say that having a vial of the blood af any random vampire gives 1 &quot;point&quot;, while finding a vial of Antediluvian blood to research gives you 50 &quot;points&quot; (to give some random numbers), fomenting to make quests for rare ingredients.<br /> <br /> Beyond mere ingredients this could abstract any sort of resource employed to develop the magick. From unearthing ancient artifacts to &quot;reverse-engineer&quot;, to deaing with powerful spirits that may provide their own insigth on the working of the universe. Resources that prove to be more adequate or interesting for the feat in question give more &quot;points&quot; to reach the breaktrough.<br /> <br /> Spells with a number of successes relative to the task should be employed in these tresholds, of course. Giving the chance to botch. But rather than giving a fixed amount of successes, the amount could depend on the task, and the task may require other rolls. For instance, summoning a spirit may be easier than dealing with it (which could require social skills, stuff to bargain, and actual Knowledges like Cosmology or Lore).<br /> <br /> Also, I would give a time needed to perform each step of the experimentation. Each independant experiment (each time the character advances the &quot;treshold&quot; of the research) would require an amount of downtime. A long amount of time, I think (months or even seasons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:12:44-07:00","id":1343058,"title":"","content":"I like the way you think!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T19:44:05-07:00","id":1344328,"title":"","content":"The old TORG RPG from West End Games had a similar setup for how the occult worked in its horror setting. It was pretty freeform; players proposed steps in the process of researching a ritual, with each subsequent step added giving greater chances of success and generating the result wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}